No point getting hot and bothered about what is just a very simple spoiler
that a few people didn't know.

Auto-pickup lets you pick up things without taking any turns.  While this isn't
an Earth-shattering spoiler, it is helpful at times.  I use it when I'm playing
fetch with my pet in a shop.  When it drops something by the shop entrance, I 
pick it up using auto-pickup, and then move back to block the door, using only 
two turns (I don't want to block that space by the entrance for longer than 
neccesary -- Fido may drop another present on the very next turn).  

Another time I use it is when I'm on the run.  If I'm out of food, I use it to
pick up food rations without breaking stride.  Also, when I'm down to my last 
few hit points, and being chased by a nasty which throws things, I use it to
pick up weapons to prevent the nasty from getting them and throwing them at
me.

Another use for autopickup is for picking up objects on teleport traps, or trap 
doors.  Aside from that, it's just a convenience.  I never leave it on -- I just 
toggle it on when I need it, and then off again right away.
